 "note": "Detection: OWLv2 (open weights), asked for each kind of thing by a short phrase; a stored sighting counts as detected when a box of that kind overlaps the true box by at least half. Recall is by the thing's size in pixels in the 960-wide render and by kind. Many pictures repeat, so 'distinct thing, place, moment' is the honest sample size. The false-alarm rate is an upper bound on hallucination: an audit found most such boxes sit on a tracked thing too small or cut to count, or on an untracked object of the home. Look-alikes: the true box is cropped and embedded, and matched against the four-view reference renders. 'Among this household's models' is what a search must decide (two things of a kind here); 'majority guess' is the score of always naming the commoner one, the trivial baseline. Below about 1,000 pixels the crops are smears a person could not judge. This household has no two identical things, so the control that should sit at chance could not be run. 40 of the 248 question times were sampled; 200 empty pictures."
